A||||3||Gold-86SE||Non-Starting Duke (explanation long, but help needed)||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||12-05-2000||09:04 PM||||<BR>Ok guys, here is one for ya. Here's the deal.<P>I have done an engine change on my 84.  I purchased an 85 Duke to place in my 84.<P>Because of the 84 wiring harness, the distributor, and sensors are 84 and the engine block and head are 85.<P>Now that everything is back in the Fiero, it won't start and I don't know why.  Please help me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000001||wilburt||12-05-2000||09:57 PM||||I would try narrowing it down by making sure I had compression, ignition, fuel. What have you checked? '85 block & head won't keep it from starting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||12-05-2000||10:49 PM||||<BR>First, Wilburt regarding your post "try narrowing it down by making sure I had compression, ignition, fuel. What have you checked?"<P>All those things were fine.<BR>Compression - just going on blind luck.<BR>Ignition - because the coil wire was removed from the coil, and tick, tick, tick goes the coil.<BR>Fuel - because fuel was being injection down the TB.<BR>What have you checked? - I thought I had checked everything, but see the update.<P><BR>Update.<P>I found out, via my wife's help - by re-investigating my manuals, that my distributor was not pointing at the number one point when TDC. Once this was placed into specs, everything started and ran fine.<P>Now, what I am finding is the oil pressure light will not go out while the engine is running.  I was thinking oil sending unit.  However, I replaced the oil pan gasket when I placed the new engine in the Fiero and considered replacing the oil pump - but did not.  Do you guys have any idea about the oil pressure light?  Man, I really don't want to pull that oil pan again.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||12-07-2000||02:15 AM||||<BR>It was the oil sending unit.<P>I assumed that the 85 oil sending unit, would work with the 84 ECM, because the plug fit.<P>Needless to say an oil sending unit for an 85 Duke will not work with an 84 ECM.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
